<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulrich I, Count of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1226–<a href="/years/1265">1265</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ulrich the Founder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulrich I, Count of Württemberg, known as the Founder, ruled Württemberg from about 1241 to 1265. In 1246 he deserted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> king Conrad IV, and as Hohenstaufen power collapsed he acquired many former royal and ducal lands and rights in Swabia, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-urach">Urach</a>. He laid the foundations of a compact territory on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a>.</p></div>
